{
  "title": "Test cyclic section controls across layouts and paragraph-stream assignments",
  "statement": "I ran the P-J-005 planted-effect calibration on 20 stationary whole-copy backgrounds per layout. At alpha 0.05, token shuffles and intact-page label permutations each rejected all 20 unplanted cases at each page count. Cyclic offsets rejected 20 of 20 unplanted cases at 31 pages, 2 of 20 at 62, and 0 of 20 at 124. Across placebo marker fractions, the cyclic rejection counts were 20 of 20 at 31 pages, 1–3 of 20 at 62, and 0 of 20 at 124. For section-exclusive marker replacement of 2.5%, 5%, 10% and 20% of eligible words, the cyclic rejection counts were 7, 18, 20 and 20 at 62 pages, and 0, 0, 14 and 20 at 124. The 31-page layout rejected all planted cases at every dose. Each page count uses one fixed layout, and the layouts are nested. They vary in section balance, ordering and paragraph structure. The calibration measures uncertainty across text-generation seeds conditional on these layouts. Differences across sizes combine page count with changes in layout.",
  "program": "J",
  "check": "Freeze additional public layouts covering multiple section-label run patterns at each page count. Cross the original two independently generated line streams with a single shared stream and a condition that fixes the paragraph-opening fraction across sections. Keep the generator stationary and the known effect and matched placebos from P-J-005. For every layout report the three nulls' rejection rates for both placebo and plant, as well as the rank of the unshifted assignment among all cyclic offsets. Compare the results at fixed page counts before recommending any null as a specificity check.",
